{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517346-romance-in-v-tm","id":1517346,"title":"Romance in V:TM","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-07T05:49:08-07:00","id":1517346,"title":"Romance in V:TM","content":"Have you ever used romance, fucked up or otherwise, in your games?<br /> <br /> What about as a motivation for NPCs?<br /> <br /> What is your favorite or least favorite romance in the WOD?<br /> <br /> I ask because it's interesting how few romances there are in V:TM as every vampire is shown to be almost universally so awful and selfish there's no romances between them beyond a handful of exceptions.<br /> <br /> It's notable that I think Lucita/Fatima/Anatole may really be the only canon one of major note.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-07T11:07:57-07:00","id":1517376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517346-romance-in-v-tm#post1517346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you ever used romance, fucked up or otherwise, in your games?<br /> <br /> What about as a motivation for NPCs?<br /> <br /> What is your favorite or least favorite romance in the WOD?<br /> <br /> I ask because it's interesting how few romances there are in V:TM as every vampire is shown to be almost universally so awful and selfish there's no romances between them beyond a handful of exceptions.<br /> <br /> It's notable that I think Lucita/Fatima/Anatole may really be the only canon one of major note.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ALL....THE....TIME..... Seriously, it's the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sAVqf2ssUEk\" target=\"_blank\">spice</a> that keeps on giving.<br /> <br /> Either developing romance itself or <i>other characters</i> guessing at a possible pairing and reacting to that chemistry (true or unfounded) they have seen, either support/ship it for all kinds of reasons good or bad or sabotage things and cause all kinds of drama due to jealousy or envy.\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> For the sake of reference i just recently started a &quot;Witnesses of Caine&quot; online chronicle, centered around a cult formed from the &quot;False Caine&quot; storyline (from BJD and Berlin by Night, with some Bloodlines, Redemption and homebrew bits mixed in). 2 of the 6 PCs(3 if one counts the &quot;roadie harem herd&quot; of the Caitiff rapper DJ) came in with romantic entanglements beforehand, two others developed their own ingame - in just three sessions, one of them a &quot;shared dreamscape of the demon sword&quot; session to boot!<br /> <br /> (And now the coterie's Toreador has a thing <i>for a torpid Forsworn Shaitan with possession/double personality issues</i>\u200b, because why not?!?! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> Honestly, i'm loving this utter band of fools.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-07-2023, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-07T11:41:03-07:00","id":1517381,"title":"","content":"My lasombra currently dating another pack member in an Sabbat game it's pretty casual and open. She exploits the vaulderie for mutual feeding as 'sex'. She initially latched onto due to him being comparatively normal and low commitment but is now caught in the tricky situation that he's surviving consistently, is superficially charming and nice to her, which she finds troubling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-07T12:22:01-07:00","id":1517383,"title":"","content":"I'm working on a Chronicle where the two Princes of a city are former enemies turned lovers.<br /> <br /> They started off on opposite sides of the Opium wars, but both fell into torpor, then came out into a world where the only things they recognized or found familiar were each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3201,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","user":"Father Enoch","date":". 07-07-2023, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-07T13:49:00-07:00","id":1517393,"title":"","content":"In my case, if it lasts a long time, it becomes a Mexican soap opera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-07T14:11:56-07:00","id":1517403,"title":"","content":"Romance in VtM tends to be either a parasitical emulation or if it is real, then it is something the PCs are actively trying to destroy between NPCs.<br /> <br /> This only gets more complicated when you consider that in the modern era romance can't exist between individuals with different levels of power, status, wealth, or experience. Such things are seen as being predatory or taking advantage of the lesser individual. With such things as an age gap and a successful career being seen as an immoral power imbalance, things like Blood Bonding, Dominate, Presence, the promise of the embrace, etc. just kind of make it an automatic non-starter.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T02:02:59-07:00","id":1517457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517346-romance-in-v-tm#post1517346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What is your favorite or least favorite romance in the WOD?<br /> <br /> It's notable that I think Lucita/Fatima/Anatole may really be the only canon one of major note.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sophie Langley and Qadir al-Asmai are another confirmed pair of Vampires who used to be lovers and close friends. The nature of their relation is mentioned in <i>Coteries of New York</i> computer game. Two Toreador Vampires who seem contrasting and different are certainly perfect, interesting, and good as representative of close bonds, devotion, romance, and trust.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T04:31:11-07:00","id":1517472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517346-romance-in-v-tm#post1517346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What is your favorite or least favorite romance in the WOD?<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Love:<br /> <br /> Absimilard and Ariker<br /> Moloch and Trolie<br /> Ma-ri-ah and Mi-ka-il<br /> The Dracon, Antonius and Micheal love tirangle\u200b<br /> Keminitri and Mithras<br /> Velya and Elaine<br /> Vykos and Ilias<br /> Beckett and Pieterzoon\u200b...? Ok the last one is unlikely really happened but fun to think about it<br /> <br /> Interestingly my least favorite are Lucita and Fatima, too forced and unrealitistic<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T09:58:44-07:00","id":1517498,"title":"","content":"My Malkavian is feeling very attracted to the descendant of his long dead best friend and he feels uncomfortable at the notion at the possibilty of dating someone that he considers almost family.<br /> <br /> Plus we have a Nosferatu in our team that is aware that a Tremere neonate has romantic feeling towards him and that threw him for a loop due to the fact of the age gap between them and she is the favorite of the local chantry leader that he is good terms with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 07-08-2023, 01:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T10:28:57-07:00","id":1517502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517346-romance-in-v-tm?p=1517498#post1517498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">we have a Nosferatu in our team that is aware that a Tremere neonate has romantic feeling towards him</div> </div> </div> </div>Gentlemen you had my curiosity ... but now you have my attention<br /> My Salubri warrior once had an affair with a Baali girl, but... I'm listening<br /> This tale sounds interesting!\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T12:45:59-07:00","id":1517512,"title":"","content":"Romance is part of the Gothic Horror genre, but I usually find most traditional RPG players are uncomfortable roleplaying it unless done at an arm's reach (establish things more OOC than IC roleplaying it, and avoid intimate details). So it's important how an ST handles it. Of course, many players of Vampire are not traditional RPG players and are more open to it, especially those who came into the hobby out of a love of vampire literature where that is very prominent. So an ST's approach needs to cater to both the general group needs and specific to each player.<br /> <br /> I let players do it however they want to approach it. It's their character. But I use some general guidelines as to how I approach it as an ST for NPCs.<br /> <br /> First, the capacity of actual love is dependent on Humanity. That is different from lust or more selfish desires. Anyone can have those, and most vampires who discover &quot;love&quot; for a particular person is more likely just driven by some kind of desire rather than love. Higher Humanity means the vampire is more capable of love, lower Humanity means it is not. Whether or not a character's &quot;romance&quot; actually turns into real &quot;love&quot; is dependent on various factors, so of course there is a spectrum. You can have romantic tropes, but not actually do romance in terms of an actual love story. Lots of vampires are skilled in appearing romantic, but that is only to groom their victims and those the opposite of actual romance.<br /> <br /> Second, actual love/romance is best done through vampire-human interaction, not between vampires. Vampires can have a relationship with one another, but over time they tend to break down into dysfunction because each of their Beasts tend to find feelings of love to be a weakness, and thus a danger to themselves that must be eliminated, and having both partners experience that doesn't lead to happy endings (I am probably influence heavily here by Michael and Sharon Payne in Chicago By Night). Mutual blood bonds and such can overcome to that some degree, but the blood bond just simulates love and is probably an anti-thesis of it. So if a player wants to experience it, as ST I would want to introduce a living human being to be their partner.<br /> <br /> Third, love is redemptive and can be a source of a vampire regaining more Humanity and increasing their Virtues. As long as it actually drives changes in behavior.<br /> <br /> Those are just general tendencies. There's nothing wrong with an elder vampire of low Humanity - or even a Path rating - somehow rediscovering true love and begin the process of clawing back their Humanity (albeit they may not succeed). That can be a great story. You can also have a high Humanity vampire reject love and begin a descent. And even inter-vampire romance can be done appropriately. Khalid having repressed love towards Elzbieta Jurofsky is something that can make the game interesting. These are just exceptions to the general rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T16:45:47-07:00","id":1517522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517346-romance-in-v-tm?p=1517512#post1517512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those are just general tendencies. There's nothing wrong with an elder vampire of low Humanity - or even a Path rating - somehow rediscovering true love and begin the process of clawing back their Humanity (albeit they may not succeed). That can be a great story. You can also have a high Humanity vampire reject love and begin a descent. And even inter-vampire romance can be done appropriately. Khalid having repressed love towards Elzbieta Jurofsky is something that can make the game interesting. These are just exceptions to the general rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that this is a good story, but I think there are very few people willing to go ahead with it, I recommend treating it as something tertiary.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T17:49:04-07:00","id":1517525,"title":"","content":"I always liked the story of the Payne couple from Chicago by Night. Most of my games have used kindred romance as more manipulative, Portia and Alicia from Chicago, but I do appreciate the relationships Chicago emphasized between various kindred. I would like to incorporate more romance in my next vampire game. I probably will order the next Renegade book that deals with it (can't remember the name).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3761-yab","name":"Yab","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T21:02:06-07:00","id":1517535,"title":"","content":"Great question <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a>. I like romance and I think it\u2019s a great plotline as long as it\u2019s not overused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T06:52:19-07:00","id":1517559,"title":"","content":"In my opinion The Fall of London is a little love story. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26793-slasher","name":"Slasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T10:54:57-07:00","id":1517573,"title":"","content":"Well the Nosferatu is very frail looking as whatever body fat he had seemingly melted away and his skin is tightly drawn on his skeleton and uses makeup and obfuscate to look more normal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T12:05:40-07:00","id":1517582,"title":"","content":"It will be a rude awakening when your Tremere develope an Auspex to see thrugh the Obfuscate <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> On the other hand, paradoxically, the love beetwn the undead are the most... pure<br /> <br /> Oxytocin is associated with trust, sexual arousal and relationship building, it's sometimes referred to as the \u201clove hormone\u201d or \u201ccuddle chemical.\u201d<br /> Contrary to what we like to say and believe, the feeling of love doesn't occur in our hearts, at least scientifically. Instead, it happens in our brain when we release hormones (oxytocin, dopamine, adrenaline, testosterone, estrogen, and vasopressin) that create a mix of feelings: euphoria, pleasure or bonding.<br /> Love technically a construct composed of both biology (e.g., hormonal shifts, release of neurotransmitters, and changes in brain activity in response to a loved one) and social meaning.<br /> Now, a dead body - or undead body - lack of these<br /> Thus any feeling is &quot;real&quot;, not affected by biology or chemicals, since the vampire's body lack these neurochemicals<br /> <br /> So, love among the dead is:<br /> A, the purest as it could be, based on real &quot;emotions&quot; of the soul\u200b, not as the victim of biology - so even a Nosferatu could be loved truly and deeply with a love that truly conquers all<br /> or<br /> B, an illusion, just the memory an undead clings in to and wants to feel, belive, but literally incapable to do it, only fools itself - wich is a very dark and tragic option to be honest\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T12:36:49-07:00","id":1517584,"title":"","content":"To be fair the neonate does have good Auspex knowledge and knows what he looks like. It\u2019s a case of weird attraction for her and it\u2019s what is surprising for the Nosferatu.<br /> <br /> He does understand it can happen as they share similar viewpoints and isn\u2019t so jaded yet by the Jyhad despite being an older ancilla.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 07-09-2023, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T12:37:59-07:00","id":1517585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517346-romance-in-v-tm?p=1517582#post1517582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It will be a rude awakening when your Tremere develope an Auspex to see thrugh the Obfuscate <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> So, love among the dead is:<br /> A, the purest as it could be, based on real &quot;emotions&quot; of the soul\u200b, not as the victim of biology - so even a Nosferatu could be loved truly and deeply with a love that truly conquers all<br /> or<br /> B, an illusion, just the memory an undead clings in to and wants to feel, belive, but literally incapable to do it, only fools itself - wich is a very dark and tragic option to be honest\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I bet in B","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T13:43:45-07:00","id":1517593,"title":"","content":"Just out of curiosity for all the posters here. Have you used a Touchstones as a romantic sub plot and how did it work out for you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T19:17:23-07:00","id":1517618,"title":"","content":"Yeah; a friend was having relationship-problems IRL, and the ST used it, (I think), in game. The PC was obsessed with a vampire-chick by the name of Cathy. So, it worked out as I ran a game of their characters, in the past as mortals, so, centuries ago, his wife was Katerina.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-10T14:44:09-07:00","id":1517657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517346-romance-in-v-tm?p=1517582#post1517582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, love among the dead is:<br /> A, the purest as it could be, based on real &quot;emotions&quot; of the soul\u200b, not as the victim of biology - so even a Nosferatu could be loved truly and deeply with a love that truly conquers all</div> </div> </div> </div>I go with that one. I enjoy love as a good, redemptive thing... as well as the concept of monsters in love (with other monsters) and love as a force of evil. Doesn't mean that vampires in love is healthy for them or those around them though.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Romance isn't popular between pcs and we rarely see pc\u00d7npc connections. <br /> There are exceptions though. I believe I mentioned them once before in a different thread, but my favourite is still the deranged Giovanni/Samedi couple. He was a sheltered necromantic prodigy (actually a rather sweet guy in a way just... completely disconnected with reality and social norms in a way that leads to arrest) and she was a walking, rotting corpse who really, really liked guns and pathology and started warming up to him when the shock wore off. It was almost sweet in a horrible, fucked in the head way.<br /> It was a courtship enhanced by the presence of a third wheel in the form of the poor Toreador<br /> <br /> <i>G: I have composed a poem.</i><br /> <i>T: *slams his drink on the table and starts counting dice*</i><br /> <i>Me: What're you doing?</i><br /> <i>T: Rolling a fucking frenzy check.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> But it's mostly just npc\u00d7npc relationships of which I have made a fair few though it's usually just background detail and the players aren't necessarily privy to then, so sometimes you accidentally piss off somebody without knowing it by messing with their SO.<br /> Also they're pretty much always vampires with other vampires, or at the very least other supernatural beings, because human-vampire romance has died a death and bores me to tears.<br /> <br /> Some of them are healthy enough, many are tragic messes, many take inspiration from Darla and Angelus and some of them I drew inspiration from the Founder and Akachi from <i>Neverwinter Nights 2: Mask of the Betrayer</i>; absolutely fucking awful monsters who nevertheless truly love each other with every fibre of their being and will spit in God's face and tear the very universe asunder in the name of that love, willing to defile and sacrifice anything and anyone for each other (even themselves) and utterly indifferent to the countless innocents who might suffer from the consequences of their actions.<br /> <br /> Due to the narrative nature of the setting, and its gothic genre typing, love (especially True Love\u2122) is a real thing and basically a force and a law of the universe. Sometimes it seems a redemptive, healing thing; sometimes it seems a ruthless insatiable hunger to be feared; usually it's both.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T10:12:00-07:00","id":1519881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517346-romance-in-v-tm?p=1517559#post1517559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my opinion The Fall of London is a little love story. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>A strange love story, but a love story of sorts I would agree with as Camden is doing everything in his power to help Mithras get his full power back and that type of stuff is what you don't normally see anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T22:46:44-07:00","id":1519932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517346-romance-in-v-tm#post1517346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you ever used romance, fucked up or otherwise, in your games?</div> </div> </div> </div>In VtM, only if I can use it as the ST to make the PC miserable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}